

🧭 Big Picture: What PySpark Is (Mental Model)

Before the roadmap, lock this idea in your head:

> PySpark is Python’s interface to Apache Spark, a distributed data processing engine designed to process large-scale data across multiple machines in parallel.



Spark is about:

Distributed computing

Fault tolerance

In-memory processing

Lazy evaluation

DataFrame & SQL abstraction


PySpark lets you write Spark code in Python, but the execution happens in the JVM.


---

🎯 Your Goal (Interview-Ready Definition)

By the end, you should be able to:

Explain why Spark exists

Explain Spark architecture clearly

Use PySpark DataFrame APIs

Write SQL-style queries in Spark

Understand performance concepts (lazy evaluation, partitioning)

Answer common interview questions confidently



